# r1108cge2 client block 1 (tools/scratch_query/cge2_run.sh client): throwaway client (eval_client.py), its mods/ with
# Common 13:51 + Compat 13:21 swapped in by the runner, single player world CGE2 = copy of the b1 world (sp_world.py,
# cheats on). Run with qrun.py client GAME this-file RES after the world is open (in game, no screen open).
# Shots go to RES/shots/; the agent reads them and the owner judges smoothness (LOOK rows).
pace 2

## CQ-CGE-02a | client boot clean, no mixin error, world joined
bootexpect Sound engine started|FIRST_CLIENT_TICK
bootreject Mixin apply failed|InvalidMixinException|InjectionError|InvalidInjectionException
bootreject (?i)(LowGravity|CreateGravity)\w*Mixin.*(error|fail|warn)
> gamemode creative
> time set noon
> gamerule doDaylightCycle false
shot joined

## CQ-CGE-02 | End: every fixed-pull type falls slowly and smoothly (client prediction matches the server)
# datapack tools/scratch_query/datapack/cge2_drop in the world: one function summons everything in one tick (typed one
# by one they spread over 35 s); the camera stands on glass (a creative player not flying falls to the ground).
# No /reload in this row: the commands typed during its hitch were lost (cge2_run.sh installs the datapack before launch).
> gamemode creative
> execute in minecraft:the_end run tp @s 14 125 9
sleep 8
> execute in minecraft:the_end run fill 12 111 7 16 111 11 minecraft:glass
> execute in minecraft:the_end run fill -2 60 -2 8 125 20 minecraft:air
> execute in minecraft:the_end run tp @s 14 112 9 facing 3 115 9
sleep 3
> function cge2:drop_end
shot end_t0
sleep 1
shot end_t1
sleep 2
shot end_t3
sleep 3
shot end_t6
look shots: the seven objects descend slowly together (about 1 block in the first second, about 5 by 3 s at most), no jumps back up between shots; owner: watch it live once for stutter or rubber-banding (none expected)

## CQ-CGE-02b | client lookup ran: the client parsed Create Gravity's list (single player)
bootexpect \[low gravity\] client biome list: 1 of 1 entries \[#minecraft:is_end;;\]
look the line appears once (it is logged on each (re)parse)

## CQ-CGE-02c | overworld: the same objects fall at vanilla speed
> execute in minecraft:overworld run tp @s 14 -30 9
sleep 8
> execute in minecraft:overworld run fill 12 -41 7 16 -41 11 minecraft:glass
> execute in minecraft:overworld run tp @s 14 -40 9 facing 3 -36 9
sleep 3
> function cge2:drop_over
shot over_t0
sleep 1
shot over_t1
look shots: vanilla fall (most of the 30 blocks in under 2 s)

## CQ-CGE-04 | End oxygen with a real player: damage without a backtank, none with one
# Create Gravity drains air slowly (about 1 a second measured), damage starts when it reaches -10. No dragon on the long wait.
# Arrive in creative and let the End chunks load before the platform: the fill fails on unloaded chunks and survival then falls.
> gamemode creative
> execute in minecraft:the_end run tp @s 32 90 0
sleep 8
> execute in minecraft:the_end run kill @e[type=minecraft:ender_dragon]
> execute in minecraft:the_end run fill 30 75 -2 34 75 2 minecraft:obsidian
> execute in minecraft:the_end run tp @s 32 76 0
sleep 3
> effect clear @s
> gamemode survival
# Air ran out about 290 s after arriving (r1108cge2), then the player died within about 25 s: wait on the log, not a clock.
waitlog ran out of air|msgId='out_of_oxygen' 420
shot oxygen_no_tank
> gamemode creative
look the waitlog line appeared (out_of_oxygen damage or death "ran out of air")

## CQ-CGE-04b | End oxygen with a backtank: no damage past the time the air would have run out
> gamemode creative
> execute in minecraft:the_end run tp @s 32 76 0
sleep 3
> effect give @s minecraft:instant_health 1 5
> item replace entity @s armor.chest with creategoggles:leather_backtank{Air:900}
sleep 2
> gamemode survival
sleep 330
> data get entity @s Health
expect has the following entity data: 20(\.0)?f
reject ran out of air
shot oxygen_tank
> gamemode creative
> item replace entity @s armor.chest with minecraft:air
look with the backtank Health stays 20 past the 290 s no-tank run-out, and the backtank air bar shows
